WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:16.015
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:24.858
Jon! And. uh...

3
00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.945
Hi. Mom. Hi. Dad.

4
00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:29.196
I'm Lara.

5
00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.907
We... We have a daughter?

6
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:32.991
Lara...

7
00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:36.161
And Jon. you're back!

8
00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:37.621
[stutters] It's Jonathan.

9
00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:39.540
And what do you mean I'm back?

10
00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:41.583
I've never been here before
in my life.

11
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.418
You were here a month ago.

12
00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.295
We saved your father. remember?

13
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.340
What are they
talking about. Lara.

14
00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:49.883
I... don't know.

15
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.176
What?

16
00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:52.719
He doesn't remember me.

17
00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:55.180
So. when we
changed the future. uh...

18
00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.808
We rewrote Jon's entire life.

19
00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:02.896
[keyboard clacking]

20
00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:09.194
You know. most people prepare
for a Pentagon inspection.

21
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:14.616
[winces. groans]

22
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.744
That's a rather... severe look.
even for you.

23
00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:21.373
Care to catch me up
on your little science project?

24
00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:25.377
It's on a need-to-know-basis.
and you don't need to know.

25
00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.672
We're supposed to be partners.
Remember?

26
00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:32.884
No. Wilson.
you work for me. remember?

27
00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:34.678
[door opens]

28
00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:38.890
Hello. Lex.

29
00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.643
Uh. Director Waller. you're...

30
00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:44.313
Yes. back in charge.

31
00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:47.190
I guess you work for her now.

32
00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:52.362
[theme music playing]

33
00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:13.925
So we've already done this?

34
00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.261
Just you. Lara wasn't here.

35
00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:18.430
But we're so happy to meet you.
[chuckles awkwardly]

36
00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.682
Wait. I didn't exist?

37
00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:22.434
Not technically.
[chuckles nervously]

38
00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:24.478
Was I. like. an accident.

39
00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:25.603
-Uh...
-[Lois gasps]

40
00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:26.813
Look. look. look.

41
00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:28.499
If... if things
didn't work out last time...

42
00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.108
-They did.
-You saved me.

43
00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.652
Stop saying that!

44
00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:32.653
That wasn't me.

45
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:35.572
It was you. A version of you.

46
00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:37.616
And you coming
back made everything better.

47
00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:39.826
Then why is my future worse?

48
00:02:42.746 --> 00:02:44.581
Beautiful day out. eh?

49
00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:46.166
The weather is pleasant.

50
00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:49.836
[sighs] So.
where are we now. Kara?

51
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.630
-The sky. over Metropolis.
-[gasps]

52
00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:52.774
[Kara] Headed to Smallville.

53
00:02:52.798 --> 00:02:55.216
No. no. I-I mean.
where are we...

54
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.510
with each other.

55
00:02:56.593 --> 00:03:01.973
Are you... Am... I... [screaming]

56
00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:04.935
[sighs in relief] Hey. did I
say something wrong up there?

57
00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.145
Jimmy Flamebirdbird.

58
00:03:07.229 --> 00:03:08.480
what do you want?

59
00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:14.653
Uh. I guess I-I-I'd wanna be
a better friend. Kara.

60
00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:16.697
I see. A friend.

61
00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:19.491
Is that all you want?

62
00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:22.119
I-I just wanna be with you.

63
00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:25.329
What do you want?

64
00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:29.376
I want to trust you...

65
00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:32.254
but I am afraid
you will leave me alone again.

66
00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.840
Kara. I...

67
00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.843
[laughing] Oh good. you're here.

68
00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:41.096
[clears throat] Kara. Jimmy.
this is Lara and Jonathan.

69
00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:43.598
From the future... [chuckles]
Again.

70
00:03:43.682 --> 00:03:45.684
Jon. you're back.

71
00:03:45.726 --> 00:03:48.478
He's not that Jon. He's... new.

72
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.563
Yes.

73
00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:51.565
Do not provoke him.

74
00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:52.691
Understood.

75
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.526
Welcome. new Jon.

76
00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:56.528
It's... Jonathan.

77
00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.946
Hey. we should get
back on mission.

78
00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:00.198
'Cause that worked out so well
for the last guy.

79
00:04:00.282 --> 00:04:01.575
Uh. what mission?

80
00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:02.951
The mission
General Lane gave us.

81
00:04:02.993 --> 00:04:05.078
Wow. Dad just can't
stop giving orders.

82
00:04:05.162 --> 00:04:08.957
Well. whatever got you here.
I'm glad to have Superboy back.

83
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.460
Don't call me Superboy.

84
00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:12.711
I'm Superman.

85
00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:16.298
Uh. we already have a Superman.
[chuckles]

86
00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.007
Do you?

87
00:04:18.048 --> 00:04:20.886
[chuckles awkwardly] Heh.
Superman this. Superboy that.

88
00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:24.723
Who wants a super slice
of Pa Kent's world famous...

89
00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:25.932
I'm done with this.

90
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.560
Or there's snickerdoodles.

91
00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.230
Jonathan.

92
00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:34.775
I-I know all of this
must be strange for you.

93
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.860
But if you need to talk...

94
00:04:36.902 --> 00:04:39.404
-I'm here to listen.
-[Jonathan chuckles]

95
00:04:39.488 --> 00:04:41.990
You think we can just
have a heart to heart?

96
00:04:42.073 --> 00:04:43.950
Maybe give me
a motivational speech.

97
00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:45.409
promise me a better tomorrow?

98
00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:48.789
Yo-You think. what.
we're just gonna play catch?

99
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:54.503
I learned to use my powers
on my own. okay?

100
00:04:54.586 --> 00:04:56.630
I defended the Earth on my own.

101
00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:59.382
Because you weren't there.

102
00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:02.010
No one was there.

103
00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:07.516
I'm not here for you
this time. Superman.

104
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.810
Stay out of my way.

105
00:05:11.937 --> 00:05:13.271
Jonathan. wait!

106
00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:17.442
-[wind blowing]
-[groans]

107
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.823
[dramatic music playing]

108
00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.866
Ah. this again. No.

109
00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:27.619
Stop!

110
00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:34.042
[Lois] You should try that.

111
00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:38.129
Pa Kent. whoo!
That man can bake. [chomps]

112
00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:42.467
Hey. don't worry about Jon...
[chuckles]

113
00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:44.553
and time loops. okay?

114
00:05:45.595 --> 00:05:47.556
Just tell me why you
and your brother are here.

115
00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:51.726
Our mission is confidential.

116
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.144
Of course it is.

117
00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:54.914
But General Lane sent us back
in time to kill Lex Luthor.

118
00:05:54.938 --> 00:05:56.439
[chokes. coughing] What?

119
00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:59.317
You traveled back in time
to commit murder?

120
00:05:59.401 --> 00:06:00.962
[sighs] We're here
to protect the future.

121
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:03.154
What kind of future
do you come from?

122
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.031
In our time Luthor commands

123
00:06:05.115 --> 00:06:08.034
a personal army of mind
controlled Kryptonian clones.

124
00:06:08.118 --> 00:06:09.286
The Eradicators.

125
00:06:09.327 --> 00:06:11.413
There has to be another way
to stop him.

126
00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:15.166
You don't have to kill Lex just
because my dad told you to.

127
00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.543
Y-Your dad?

128
00:06:16.626 --> 00:06:17.919
Yeah. General Lane.

129
00:06:17.961 --> 00:06:19.921
-That's not who...
-Salt and pepper crewcut.

130
00:06:20.005 --> 00:06:21.214
always giving orders.

131
00:06:21.298 --> 00:06:24.759
No. You told us
to kill Lex Luthor.

132
00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:26.428
You're General Lane.

133
00:06:27.262 --> 00:06:28.346
[chokes]

134
00:06:29.514 --> 00:06:33.602
As you can see. Lexcorp
is paving the way to a safer.

135
00:06:33.685 --> 00:06:35.437
more secure Metropolis with...

136
00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.521
Save it. Luthor.

137
00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:37.647
[Wilson chuckles]

138
00:06:38.607 --> 00:06:40.692
Wilson. you're still here.

139
00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:43.111
My apologies. Mr. Luthor.

140
00:06:43.194 --> 00:06:45.030
But why don't you show
Director Waller

141
00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:46.990
your latest project?

142
00:06:47.699 --> 00:06:48.950
Ah...

143
00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:51.578
It's... still in its infancy.
not ready for review.

144
00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:54.998
-But over here...
-I insist.

145
00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:57.250
Very well.

146
00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.214
Director Waller.
allow me to present...

147
00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.552
Project Eradicator.

148
00:07:07.636 --> 00:07:09.054
[Slade and Waller gasp]

149
00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:12.891
Once complete. this weapon
will put humanity back on top

150
00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:15.268
as the world's dominant species.

151
00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:18.104
Created from Superman's
own living tissue.

152
00:07:18.188 --> 00:07:21.066
Eradicator self-repairs.
self-evolves.

153
00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:25.737
and will function under my
complete direct mental control.

154
00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:27.447
Mental control?

155
00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.532
The hardware is not finished.
but once it is.

156
00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:31.993
the Luthor gray matter
I put in Eradicator's brain

157
00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:34.412
will let me
control him with mine.

158
00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:38.166
You put a piece of your brain
inside that thing?

159
00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:39.668
That's all I need to see.

160
00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:41.169
Shut it down. Luthor.

161
00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:43.088
Wait. you don't understand.

162
00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:45.048
The Eradicator
will revolutionize...

163
00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.509
No. you don't understand.

164
00:07:47.592 --> 00:07:50.095
I'm not just shutting down
Project Eradicator.

165
00:07:50.178 --> 00:07:54.432
I'm shutting down all of
Lexcorp. effective immediately.

166
00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:55.976
[suspenseful music
intensifies. stops]

167
00:07:56.058 --> 00:07:57.769
[both sigh]

168
00:07:57.852 --> 00:07:59.688
Welp. I'm a horrible parent.

169
00:07:59.771 --> 00:08:00.689
Me too.

170
00:08:00.772 --> 00:08:02.023
Poor Jonathan.

171
00:08:02.065 --> 00:08:04.275
Jonathan?
I'm talking about Lara.

172
00:08:04.359 --> 00:08:07.320
Ugh. you think you're doing
your best as a mother. but...

173
00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:08.613
Well. at least you were there.

174
00:08:08.697 --> 00:08:11.574
I somehow missed our kids'
lives two times in a row.

175
00:08:11.616 --> 00:08:12.867
Maybe that's it.

176
00:08:12.951 --> 00:08:14.452
Maybe I'm the problem.

177
00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:17.205
I'm the reason Lara
turned out this way.

178
00:08:17.247 --> 00:08:18.415
Wait. what's wrong with Lara?

179
00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:19.791
Wait...

180
00:08:19.874 --> 00:08:22.127
where is Lara?

181
00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:24.129
[Lex] Director Waller.

182
00:08:24.212 --> 00:08:27.757
I-I'm... I'm working
for the good of humankind here.

183
00:08:27.799 --> 00:08:29.134
[Waller] Out of my way. Luthor.

184
00:08:30.427 --> 00:08:31.469
You see this?

185
00:08:31.553 --> 00:08:34.264
That's a prototype
time travel device.

186
00:08:34.304 --> 00:08:37.392
Imagine what we could do
once it's complete.

187
00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:39.519
Yo-You'll... You'll be able
to go back to the past

188
00:08:39.602 --> 00:08:42.063
and stop your enemies
before they even strike.

189
00:08:42.147 --> 00:08:43.857
I've made my decision. Luthor.

190
00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.484
Listen.
I've seen what's out there.

191
00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:48.528
Superman's not even
the worst of it.

192
00:08:48.611 --> 00:08:51.823
There are... things waiting
in space that...

193
00:08:51.906 --> 00:08:56.119
Superman put his life
on the line when we needed him.

194
00:08:56.161 --> 00:08:58.955
I'll take space aliens
over you any day.

195
00:08:58.997 --> 00:09:03.168
You've not only failed to live
up to Checkmate's expectations.

196
00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:05.378
you don't even look
after your own.

197
00:09:07.881 --> 00:09:09.424
You.

198
00:09:09.507 --> 00:09:10.633
-[blasts]
-Ahhh!

199
00:09:14.095 --> 00:09:16.181
And who is this young lady?

200
00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:17.682
I'm here for Luthor.

201
00:09:19.142 --> 00:09:21.770
No. stop. stop!
I'm... I'm... I'm... [panting]

202
00:09:21.853 --> 00:09:23.563
I-I'm just a scientist.

203
00:09:23.646 --> 00:09:25.106
[Lara] Just a scientist?

204
00:09:26.274 --> 00:09:28.860
[scoffs] You're the end
of the world.

205
00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:29.986
[grunts]

206
00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.906
[dramatic music playing]

207
00:09:32.989 --> 00:09:35.325
[gasps. grunts]

208
00:09:37.869 --> 00:09:39.454
[groans]

209
00:09:41.664 --> 00:09:42.832
[pants]

210
00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:49.798
-[roaring]
-[bones cracking]

211
00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:53.676
[Lara screaming]

212
00:09:55.553 --> 00:09:58.223
Just like Lara
to rush headlong into things.

213
00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:01.101
Always trying to be mommy's
perfect little soldier.

214
00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.021
Sorry. kids.

215
00:10:05.063 --> 00:10:06.397
Whole site's locked down.

216
00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:08.983
No one gets past me...

217
00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:12.654
Especially Kryptonians.

218
00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:13.696
Where's Lara?

219
00:10:13.738 --> 00:10:15.073
Lara?

220
00:10:15.115 --> 00:10:17.992
Is that the super-powered
teenager who tried to kill Lex?

221
00:10:18.076 --> 00:10:19.345
They took the fight underground.

222
00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:21.746
-[Clark] Who's they?
-[Clark. Lois. and Jimmy gasp]

223
00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:26.626
[all screaming]

224
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:28.753
[both screaming]

225
00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:31.840
You okay. Smallville?

226
00:10:31.923 --> 00:10:34.425
Yeah. the sewage broke my fall.

227
00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:35.510
Oh. good.

228
00:10:38.138 --> 00:10:39.973
[Clark] Is Lara down here?

229
00:10:40.056 --> 00:10:41.933
She must be.
And the sooner we find her.

230
00:10:42.016 --> 00:10:43.077
the sooner
we can get out of here.

231
00:10:43.101 --> 00:10:44.477
[loud thud]

232
00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:46.062
[Clark] Lara?

233
00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.783
[both gasp]

234
00:11:00.451 --> 00:11:02.429
For a second. I thought
there was a monster down here...

235
00:11:02.453 --> 00:11:05.790
Shh! There is
a monster down here.

236
00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:12.172
Kal-El? Lois?

237
00:11:12.255 --> 00:11:15.091
Let's split up. We'll find them
faster that way.

238
00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:17.177
That is unwise. Jonathan.

239
00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.262
The lead in this facility
is disrupting the...

240
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:20.972
Whatever.
I don't need your permission.

241
00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:24.392
[groans]

242
00:11:25.602 --> 00:11:29.314
Kal-El. Lois Lane.
can you hear me?

243
00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:35.320
-[Jonathan grunts]
-Jonathan?

244
00:11:36.654 --> 00:11:37.822
[groans]

245
00:11:37.906 --> 00:11:39.324
[glass breaking]

246
00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:44.495
[roars]

247
00:11:47.498 --> 00:11:48.750
[Clark and Lois] Help!

248
00:11:53.796 --> 00:11:55.006
[soft roar]

249
00:11:55.048 --> 00:11:56.132
[groans]

250
00:11:56.174 --> 00:11:57.217
[roars]

251
00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.511
[Jonathan] No. no. no. no. no!
[shrieks]

252
00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:01.763
Jonathan!

253
00:12:02.722 --> 00:12:03.765
Lara. wait.

254
00:12:08.478 --> 00:12:09.979
[panting] Which way?

255
00:12:10.021 --> 00:12:11.189
I-I-I think she went...

256
00:12:11.272 --> 00:12:12.440
-[snarls]
-[both gasp]

257
00:12:12.523 --> 00:12:13.733
[roaring]

258
00:12:18.196 --> 00:12:20.073
Where's my brother?

259
00:12:20.156 --> 00:12:21.616
[Lara grunting]

260
00:12:24.619 --> 00:12:25.662
[Lois] Ahhh!

261
00:12:26.621 --> 00:12:29.666
[both grunt]

262
00:12:33.628 --> 00:12:34.963
[grunts]

263
00:12:40.635 --> 00:12:43.638
[roars]

264
00:12:48.393 --> 00:12:49.310
[Clark] Lara!

265
00:12:49.394 --> 00:12:50.687
[Lara grunts]

266
00:12:50.728 --> 00:12:52.063
What is that thing?

267
00:12:52.105 --> 00:12:55.149
It's an Eradicator.
But... this one is different.

268
00:12:55.191 --> 00:12:56.943
[whirring]

269
00:12:57.026 --> 00:12:59.404
[Jonathan] Back off!

270
00:13:03.574 --> 00:13:05.034
[grunts]

271
00:13:05.076 --> 00:13:06.411
[grunts]

272
00:13:06.494 --> 00:13:08.204
Lara. you're hurt. Get back!

273
00:13:08.246 --> 00:13:10.081
Don't listen to her.
Get behind him.

274
00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:12.792
Lara. listen to me.

275
00:13:12.875 --> 00:13:13.918
[roars]

276
00:13:15.586 --> 00:13:17.088
[dramatic music intensifies]

277
00:13:17.171 --> 00:13:18.631
No!

278
00:13:18.715 --> 00:13:21.342
[roaring]

279
00:13:24.053 --> 00:13:25.096
[train honks]

280
00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:32.854
Stay away from my family.

281
00:13:33.938 --> 00:13:35.773
[roars]

282
00:13:35.857 --> 00:13:37.775
[roars]

283
00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:40.403
[upbeat rock music playing]

284
00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:42.780
[grunting]

285
00:13:48.411 --> 00:13:49.996
[glass breaking]

286
00:13:57.754 --> 00:13:58.796
[gasping]

287
00:14:06.054 --> 00:14:07.805
Kids. wait!

288
00:14:07.847 --> 00:14:10.933
Our children...
are so disrespectful.

289
00:14:11.476 --> 00:14:12.894
Come on. this way.

290
00:14:14.604 --> 00:14:17.023
Bring your monster
to heel. Luthor.

291
00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:20.318
I-I... I can't stop it.

292
00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.028
Don't you two share a brain?

293
00:14:23.071 --> 00:14:26.616
What happened
to "direct mental control?"

294
00:14:26.657 --> 00:14:29.786
[Lex] I already told you.
the system is incomplete.

295
00:14:29.827 --> 00:14:31.871
It won't respond to my commands.

296
00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:35.415
Eradicator's in control.

297
00:14:36.751 --> 00:14:38.252
-[dramatic music playing]
-[roars]

298
00:14:38.336 --> 00:14:39.754
[Supergirl grunts]

299
00:14:41.297 --> 00:14:43.591
[grunts. screaming]

300
00:14:49.472 --> 00:14:50.515
Lara!

301
00:14:51.516 --> 00:14:52.558
[grunts]

302
00:15:00.191 --> 00:15:02.026
Lara! Lara!

303
00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.487
-[roars]
-[grunts]

304
00:15:05.738 --> 00:15:11.035
I am your opponent. [grunts]

305
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:18.584
Ahhh!

306
00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:21.170
[grunting]

307
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.720
[grunting]

308
00:15:37.854 --> 00:15:39.147
[grunting]

309
00:15:42.442 --> 00:15:44.360
[Jonathan]
He's evolving too fast for us.

310
00:15:44.402 --> 00:15:46.863
We've... We've lost.

311
00:15:47.822 --> 00:15:50.366
Just like that other Jonathan.

312
00:15:50.408 --> 00:15:52.660
There's... There's nothing
we can do.

313
00:15:52.743 --> 00:15:53.661
Ow!

314
00:15:53.744 --> 00:15:54.787
You are not the only one

315
00:15:54.871 --> 00:15:57.081
who has seen
a different world. Jonathan.

316
00:15:57.123 --> 00:15:59.792
I have seen other futures.

317
00:15:59.876 --> 00:16:02.879
We can still choose
a better tomorrow.

318
00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.215
[growling]

319
00:16:06.257 --> 00:16:08.050
[roars]

320
00:16:09.177 --> 00:16:10.303
Stay here.

321
00:16:10.386 --> 00:16:11.888
I'll show you.

322
00:16:13.764 --> 00:16:14.849
[grunting]

323
00:16:23.858 --> 00:16:25.568
She's alone with that thing.

324
00:16:27.612 --> 00:16:28.821
Clark. you can't.

325
00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.992
That's a job... for Superman.

326
00:16:35.745 --> 00:16:37.830
-[Supergirl grunting]
-[roars]

327
00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:42.168
[grunting]

328
00:16:42.251 --> 00:16:43.503
[roars]

329
00:16:43.586 --> 00:16:46.547
[dramatic music playing]

330
00:16:46.964 --> 00:16:48.174
[grunting]

331
00:16:52.428 --> 00:16:54.639
[roaring]

332
00:16:55.556 --> 00:16:59.936
[screaming]

333
00:17:01.979 --> 00:17:03.648
[whirring]

334
00:17:04.357 --> 00:17:05.650
No.

335
00:17:09.904 --> 00:17:14.617
[screaming]

336
00:17:27.505 --> 00:17:29.840
Kara! Kara.

337
00:17:31.259 --> 00:17:32.343
Why?

338
00:17:32.385 --> 00:17:33.427
You...

339
00:17:34.845 --> 00:17:36.764
are my better tomorrow.

340
00:17:44.438 --> 00:17:45.940
[wind blows]

341
00:17:51.028 --> 00:17:52.196
Kara!

342
00:17:55.199 --> 00:17:56.325
Jonathan!

343
00:17:56.367 --> 00:17:58.035
[wind whooshes]

344
00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:00.913
What?

345
00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:05.626
Not again.

346
00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:07.670
My family needs me.

347
00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:10.339
They need me.

348
00:18:10.965 --> 00:18:16.053
[Kryptonian voices whispering]

349
00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:19.098
[wind whooshes]

350
00:18:24.687 --> 00:18:25.896
Enough of this.

351
00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.231
[growls]

352
00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:30.234
[screams]

353
00:18:30.276 --> 00:18:31.736
[roars]

354
00:18:31.819 --> 00:18:33.779
[dramatic music playing]

355
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.243
[grunts]

356
00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.546
[growls]

357
00:18:50.588 --> 00:18:51.756
[Jonathan grunts]

358
00:18:58.471 --> 00:18:59.639
[evil laughter]

359
00:18:59.722 --> 00:19:02.475
You... lose.

360
00:19:02.558 --> 00:19:07.271
[fading evil laughter]

361
00:19:07.313 --> 00:19:08.898
[music stops]

362
00:19:12.109 --> 00:19:13.194
Kara!

363
00:19:13.277 --> 00:19:14.403
Kara. please!

364
00:19:17.281 --> 00:19:19.950
I am... too late.

365
00:19:20.576 --> 00:19:21.702
She's not.

366
00:19:22.703 --> 00:19:24.163
She's not waking up.

367
00:19:27.124 --> 00:19:28.125
[Lois] Jonathan...

368
00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:31.337
Are you okay?

369
00:19:33.923 --> 00:19:35.716
I couldn't stop it.

370
00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.095
Eradicator is loose
in the time stream.

371
00:19:43.724 --> 00:19:46.477
So. who am I arresting?

372
00:19:46.519 --> 00:19:48.062
What?

373
00:19:48.145 --> 00:19:50.439
We haven't been
properly introduced.

374
00:19:50.481 --> 00:19:53.484
Amanda Waller. Pentagon.

375
00:19:53.526 --> 00:19:56.195
Director Waller. the kids
were just following orders.

376
00:19:56.278 --> 00:19:57.697
They were sent here
from the future

377
00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.157
to stop Lex
from unleashing that monster.

378
00:20:00.241 --> 00:20:05.037
Uh... I was defending myself
from an assassination.

379
00:20:05.121 --> 00:20:08.249
The prototype was never meant
to be active at this stage.

380
00:20:08.332 --> 00:20:11.877
It-It's her fault.
That... th-th-tha-that...

381
00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:15.965
[groans]

382
00:20:16.006 --> 00:20:18.259
Slade. you tell them.
You saw everything.

383
00:20:18.342 --> 00:20:20.678
Y-You know what I was
trying to accomplish.

384
00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.430
What we were trying to do.

385
00:20:24.682 --> 00:20:27.059
I tried to tell you. Alex.

386
00:20:28.728 --> 00:20:29.812
[Waller] Wilson...

387
00:20:30.354 --> 00:20:32.231
book Lex Luthor.

388
00:20:32.314 --> 00:20:35.443
We'll sort out our...
new guests later.

389
00:20:37.737 --> 00:20:39.405
What are we gonna do. Clark?

390
00:20:39.488 --> 00:20:40.656
Kara.

391
00:20:40.698 --> 00:20:41.699
the kids.

392
00:20:41.782 --> 00:20:43.451
the monster...

393
00:20:43.534 --> 00:20:45.202
How are we gonna fix this?

394
00:20:45.286 --> 00:20:48.456
I... I think I know
where my powers are.

395
00:20:48.539 --> 00:20:49.957
I think I can get them back.

396
00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.918
[gasps] You can
bring back Superman?

397
00:20:53.002 --> 00:20:54.628
I think so. but I...

398
00:20:54.712 --> 00:20:56.130
I'll have to leave.

399
00:20:57.256 --> 00:20:58.466
For a little while.

400
00:20:58.549 --> 00:20:59.633
Clark. no.

401
00:20:59.717 --> 00:21:01.236
No. you can't leave me alone
with these kids.

402
00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.721
I'll fail them.
We know I fail them.

403
00:21:03.763 --> 00:21:06.724
You aren't the person
who sent them here. Lois.

404
00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:08.267
They need the real you.

405
00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.351
This you.

406
00:21:09.393 --> 00:21:11.228
But I need you. Clark.

407
00:21:11.312 --> 00:21:13.522
Our whole future
is getting ripped away.

408
00:21:13.564 --> 00:21:15.065
First Jon and now...

409
00:21:16.692 --> 00:21:19.195
I'm only going away
for a little while.

410
00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.782
We can't save the kids.

411
00:21:22.865 --> 00:21:24.825
We... We can't save
the future...

412
00:21:25.534 --> 00:21:26.577
without Superman.

413
00:21:33.918 --> 00:21:35.127
[Lois] Promise me. then.

414
00:21:35.211 --> 00:21:37.880
Promise me. Clark.
that you'll come back.

415
00:21:37.922 --> 00:21:39.632
[shrieks]

416
00:21:39.715 --> 00:21:43.594
[grunting]

417
00:21:44.762 --> 00:21:46.472
[Clark] I promise.

418
00:21:46.555 --> 00:21:49.475
[suspenseful music playing]

419
00:21:55.773 --> 00:21:58.734
[theme music playing]
